# Line endings are pinned to LF in the working copy, not just in the repo.
#
# Git stores LF and, with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default), hands the
# working copy CRLF on checkout. The tests read the real index.html and sw.js
# and match on \n, so a rebase, pull or fresh clone on Windows produced a
# working copy every test crashed on. The tests normalise line endings at the
# read as well — this is the other half, so that anything else reading these
# files sees what the repo actually contains.
*           text=auto eol=lf
*.png       binary
*.ico       binary
